From: skrimix <skrimix.git@fastmail.org>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: add OnePlus Pad 2 PPS charging

Charge from third-party USB-PD PPS adapters through the two SC8547A charge
pumps, following the OEM Android policy: one session per insertion when the
battery is eligible, the observed fixed 5 V / input suspend / voltage ramp
/ staggered pump start sequence, the board's SOC and temperature curves,
high-temperature ladder, full checks and timeout, and the OEM gauge,
connector, battery current and input current limits. Sessions stop before
suspend, reboot and OTG changes. While a session holds the PMIC charger's
input suspended, the firmware reports Not charging; report Charging
instead, as the OEM's own status policy does.

Enabled by oneplus,charge-pumps on the pmic-glink node. sysfs pps_charging
switches it off and on, and pps_active reads 1 while a session runs, with
a uevent on each change, so that userspace can inhibit system sleep, which
would end the session. debugfs pps_control shows the session and accepts
"stop", and pps_limit_ma caps the current at 1000-5000 mA.
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
